WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.545
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:14.815 --> 00:17.015
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

3
00:36.425 --> 00:38.086
Welcome to Sunny Mart. How may I help you?

4
02:18.426 --> 02:22.426
Help...help me!

5
03:35.809 --> 03:36.856
Which one do you want, Nava?

6
03:53.945 --> 03:54.594
Got it.

7
03:57.648 --> 03:59.382
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

8
04:04.577 --> 04:05.312
Excuse me.

9
04:06.530 --> 04:07.449
Could you please get in line?

10
04:07.664 --> 04:08.785
I’ll just pay real quick.

11
04:12.991 --> 04:13.671
Fine, whatever.

12
04:20.812 --> 04:22.734
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

13
04:27.218 --> 04:28.663
You’re off to school early today.

14
04:30.960 --> 04:32.304
I don't need the bag.

15
04:34.632 --> 04:36.296
Oh, aren’t you going to work today?

16
04:41.921 --> 04:44.663
Would you like some shumai or steamed buns? They’re half price right now.

17
05:02.249 --> 05:04.421
Are you excited to be starting elementary school, Nava?

18
05:09.890 --> 05:12.491
I’ll put this doll in your bag, so it can keep you company.

19
05:19.413 --> 05:20.398
Remember to say hello to your teacher, dear.

20
05:43.757 --> 05:44.347
Metha?

21
05:46.616 --> 05:47.913
You really are here.

22
05:52.702 --> 05:53.778
I thought you said you’d quit.

23
06:02.680 --> 06:05.187
I saw a clip of you yesterday.

24
06:09.765 --> 06:10.695
You’re getting famous now, huh?

25
06:21.755 --> 06:23.161
The guy was smoking where smoking’s prohibited.

26
06:24.263 --> 06:25.528
There was even a sign.

27
06:27.427 --> 06:28.739
I get that you meant well.

28
06:30.083 --> 06:32.466
But don’t you think you went a bit overboard?

29
06:33.466 --> 06:34.606
You got him fired, man.

30
06:36.552 --> 06:38.372
He wouldn't if he’d followed the rules in the first place.

31
06:40.388 --> 06:42.849
If it were that simple, why would we even need the police?

32
06:46.356 --> 06:46.981
See you around.

33
06:47.931 --> 06:48.485
Hey.

34
06:51.419 --> 06:52.426
Seriously.

35
06:54.310 --> 06:56.020
don’t you ever think about becoming a cop again?

36
07:01.770 --> 07:03.263
I wouldn’t be able to change anything anyway.

37
07:08.731 --> 07:09.544
Come on, man.

38
07:10.247 --> 07:12.661
But at least you’d still make a living, right?

39
07:58.802 --> 08:00.123
Amazing!

40
08:00.527 --> 08:01.293
Yeah!

41
08:02.316 --> 08:03.139
Yeah!

42
08:03.164 --> 08:04.483
Daddy, you’re amazing!

43
08:04.508 --> 08:06.772
You’re Super Dad. You can do anything!

44
08:06.829 --> 08:07.778
If there’s a Super Dad,

45
08:07.802 --> 08:10.835
then there must be a Super Nava, too!

46
08:12.579 --> 08:13.477
Super Nava!

47
09:11.524 --> 09:13.644
(Drop by Sunny, Happy Every Day.)

48
09:14.789 --> 09:17.399
Hello. Welcome to Sunny Mart!

49
09:24.793 --> 09:29.966
(Urgently hiring night shift staff!)

50
09:36.520 --> 09:39.679
Ten thousand a night, not a month?

51
09:48.751 --> 09:49.605
Yes.

52
09:50.366 --> 09:54.304
The night-shift staff get paid 10,000 baht per night.

53
09:55.093 --> 09:56.221
That’s correct.

54
09:57.034 --> 10:00.348
And the best part is, we pay you daily.

55
10:00.704 --> 10:03.961
As soon as you finish your shift, you get paid.

56
10:07.758 --> 10:09.267
The job must be really tough, right?

57
10:09.345 --> 10:11.303
No, it's not.

58
10:11.327 --> 10:13.963
It’s just like working at any other convenience store.

59
10:14.416 --> 10:17.492
You just have to follow all the employee rules.

60
10:21.680 --> 10:22.843
Just follow the rules?

61
10:25.456 --> 10:28.541
If you’re interested, come apply.

62
10:28.565 --> 10:30.729
We’re urgently hiring right now.

63
10:34.685 --> 10:35.735
Ten thousand a night.

64
10:38.073 --> 10:39.058
I’ll think about it.

65
10:40.602 --> 10:42.043
All right. See you.

66
11:10.357 --> 11:11.744
Mr. Metha.

67
11:12.886 --> 11:14.533
Ever since you borrowed money,

68
11:14.841 --> 11:16.490
you’ve been awfully hard to get ahold of.

69
11:17.779 --> 11:18.518
Sir.

70
11:19.995 --> 11:21.018
I was just about to call you.

71
11:23.315 --> 11:24.292
But you know

72
11:25.017 --> 11:27.604
you’re already two days late paying me back, right?

73
11:30.642 --> 11:32.366
I’ll find a way to pay you back.

74
11:35.003 --> 11:36.171
Mr. Metha.

75
11:37.417 --> 11:41.212
I’ve been lending money for over 10 years.

76
11:41.767 --> 11:42.863
You know what?

77
11:43.673 --> 11:48.734
People who are desperate all act exactly like you do.

78
11:49.774 --> 11:50.607
Hey.

79
11:58.068 --> 11:59.261
Metha!

80
12:00.071 --> 12:00.829
Go after him!

81
12:05.393 --> 12:06.583
You’re pretty good at running away, huh?

82
12:06.620 --> 12:08.028
You think I wouldn’t catch up with you?

83
12:09.525 --> 12:10.282
The lighter.

84
12:26.750 --> 12:28.453
Why did you think you could get away from me?

85
12:29.801 --> 12:30.308
Huh?

86
12:31.108 --> 12:31.833
Huh?

87
12:34.827 --> 12:35.461
Tomorrow.

88
12:36.917 --> 12:38.075
I’ll get the money for you tomorrow.

89
12:39.200 --> 12:39.936
I swear.

90
12:41.765 --> 12:42.554
Sure.

91
12:43.262 --> 12:44.968
I’m a man who gives people chances.

92
12:50.056 --> 12:52.264
But if you can’t pay tomorrow,

93
12:53.194 --> 12:55.904
it won't just end here.

94
12:57.246 --> 12:58.105
Got it?

95
13:01.659 --> 13:02.698
Right.

96
13:05.000 --> 13:05.864
This motorcycle.

97
13:06.472 --> 13:07.709
I’ll take it as interest on the debt.

98
13:48.744 --> 13:53.430
(Urgently hiring night shift staff!)

99
14:18.086 --> 14:18.918
Here.

100
14:21.184 --> 14:25.159
Metha Triwikul. Goes by Metha.

101
14:25.613 --> 14:26.635
Age 34.

102
14:30.495 --> 14:31.380
Okay.

103
14:32.100 --> 14:33.162
You meet all the requirements.

104
14:34.051 --> 14:35.460
You can start tonight.

105
14:39.518 --> 14:41.584
Wait, I got the job already?

106
14:41.994 --> 14:42.501
That’s right.

107
14:43.296 --> 14:46.309
We’re short-staffed on the night shift right now.

108
14:46.633 --> 14:50.378
If you can start right away, we’d like you to start tonight.

109
14:52.927 --> 14:54.826
Is anything stopping you?

110
14:55.097 --> 14:56.441
Oh, no problem at all.

111
14:57.321 --> 14:58.612
I can start tonight.

112
14:58.804 --> 15:00.228
Great.

113
15:00.645 --> 15:03.149
Our night-shift staff start at midnight.

114
15:03.174 --> 15:05.918
I’d like you to arrive ten minutes

115
15:05.942 --> 15:06.828
before your shift begins.

116
15:07.240 --> 15:08.664
That’s the first rule

117
15:08.968 --> 15:10.218
for night-shift employees.

118
15:10.916 --> 15:12.276
Make sure you remember it.

119
15:16.352 --> 15:16.923
Thank you.

120
15:30.892 --> 15:31.739
Nava.

121
15:33.474 --> 15:35.080
I might not be home with you tonight.

122
15:47.227 --> 15:48.523
Hello!

123
15:55.420 --> 15:56.273
Hello.

124
15:57.116 --> 16:00.454
I came right over as soon as you called.

125
16:00.892 --> 16:03.110
Well, I’ve switched to working nights lately.

126
16:04.166 --> 16:06.947
Could you look after Nava until 6 am?

127
16:08.042 --> 16:10.927
Wow, until 6 am?

128
16:12.441 --> 16:14.671
My back’s been hurting lately.

129
16:14.695 --> 16:16.447
Sleeping somewhere unfamiliar might...

130
16:16.471 --> 16:17.241
I’ll pay you.

131
16:18.963 --> 16:21.321
Oh, we’re practically family!

132
16:21.577 --> 16:23.257
Just give me 500 baht.

133
16:35.587 --> 16:37.741
Is 400 baht okay? That’s all I have.

134
16:42.298 --> 16:43.624
All right, then.

135
16:45.080 --> 16:46.654
Four hundred it is.

136
16:47.480 --> 16:49.437
I’m only charging you that because we’re neighbors.

137
16:49.461 --> 16:51.406
We’ve got to help each other out.

138
16:55.185 --> 16:55.980
Nava.

139
16:56.758 --> 16:58.518
You’ll stay with me today, okay?

140
16:59.105 --> 17:00.764
I’ll hurry home as soon as my shift ends.

141
17:01.430 --> 17:02.860
Just hurry up and go.

142
17:42.808 --> 17:43.758
That scared me.

143
17:47.599 --> 17:48.591
What is it doing here?

144
18:04.514 --> 18:05.912
Welcome to Sunny Mart!

145
18:18.945 --> 18:19.777
Wow.

146
18:21.460 --> 18:22.758
You look nice.

147
18:24.654 --> 18:25.580
Here you go.

148
18:26.433 --> 18:27.937
Your employment contract.

149
18:28.790 --> 18:30.086
I’ve got everything ready for you.

150
18:30.560 --> 18:33.413
But before you sign, I must advise you

151
18:33.690 --> 18:37.680
to read every detail of the contract carefully.

152
18:37.932 --> 18:39.907
This is to protect your own interests.

153
18:39.931 --> 18:43.569
Especially the 13 rules for night-shift employees.

154
18:45.357 --> 18:47.290
If you can’t remember them all,

155
18:47.314 --> 18:49.378
I’ve posted them by the counter.

156
18:49.517 --> 18:52.781
I recommend memorizing every single one.

157
18:54.160 --> 18:55.232
Because here...

158
18:55.824 --> 18:56.496
The rules

159
18:56.965 --> 18:58.634
are a matter of life and death.

160
19:01.345 --> 19:04.330
If you have any questions, just ask.

161
19:09.205 --> 19:11.858
Will I really get 10,000 baht per night?

162
19:14.384 --> 19:15.580
Absolutely.

163
19:16.439 --> 19:19.048
Don’t worry. It’s right here in the contract.

164
19:19.624 --> 19:20.697
It's 10,000 baht

165
19:21.379 --> 19:23.373
as long as you stay for the full shift.

166
19:31.736 --> 19:32.557
Deal.

167
19:41.619 --> 19:43.914
Okay, all done.

168
19:44.457 --> 19:46.958
Let’s take a photo for your employee ID.

169
19:47.541 --> 19:48.759
Mr. Metha, please wait over there.

170
19:52.133 --> 19:54.532
Right by that wall. Over there.

171
20:05.309 --> 20:06.043
Look at the camera.

172
20:06.679 --> 20:09.139
One, two, three.

173
20:19.064 --> 20:20.120
Mr. Metha.

174
20:22.369 --> 20:26.153
Our store has individual lockers for each employee.

175
20:26.478 --> 20:30.132
You can put your personal belongings in here.

176
20:30.157 --> 20:32.152
Your mobile phone goes here, too.

177
20:34.892 --> 20:36.125
Dear’s just arrived.

178
20:38.378 --> 20:39.060
Dear.

179
20:39.844 --> 20:43.151
This is Metha, our new night-shift employee.

180
20:43.631 --> 20:44.916
And this is Dear.

181
20:45.321 --> 20:48.607
She’s been on the night shift longer than anyone else.

182
20:49.028 --> 20:51.284
Dear will train you.

183
20:51.547 --> 20:52.754
No need, Cherd.

184
20:53.064 --> 20:54.818
Who knows if he’ll even make it through tonight?

185
20:56.705 --> 20:59.244
Why would you say that, Dear? Look at him first.

186
20:59.340 --> 21:01.252
He looks capable.

187
21:01.413 --> 21:04.464
He might handle the customers better than we expect.

188
21:14.841 --> 21:16.857
Rule number 1 for night-shift employees.

189
21:17.009 --> 21:20.665
You must arrive ten minutes before your shift starts.

190
21:25.994 --> 21:27.192
It’s only a minute.

191
21:28.079 --> 21:29.600
I’d still make it on time for work.

192
21:29.803 --> 21:30.667
You know

193
21:31.733 --> 21:35.957
how serious the consequences are if you break the rules.

194
21:36.135 --> 21:38.535
Yes, I know.

195
21:39.234 --> 21:41.293
So annoying.

196
21:43.758 --> 21:44.529
Metha.

197
21:45.556 --> 21:48.558
This is Bird, our other night-shift employee.

198
22:42.328 --> 22:43.242
Rule number one.

199
22:44.028 --> 22:47.548
Night-shift working hours are from midnight to six am.

200
22:47.958 --> 22:49.645
Please arrive 10 minutes early.

201
22:50.097 --> 22:51.965
You must not leave the convenience store premises

202
22:51.989 --> 22:53.011
during your shift.

203
22:58.675 --> 22:59.737
Move. You’re in the way.

204
23:08.049 --> 23:08.883
Rule number five.

205
23:09.465 --> 23:11.959
At least one must remain at the counter at all times.

206
23:12.596 --> 23:13.385
The counter must not be left unattended

207
23:13.409 --> 23:14.381
for more than three minutes.

208
23:24.993 --> 23:25.646
Rule number 10.

209
23:26.587 --> 23:27.693
No expired products

210
23:27.717 --> 23:29.599
or foreign objects may be left inside the store.

211
23:30.232 --> 23:31.334
If found, dispose of them.

212
23:47.038 --> 23:48.554
What should I be doing?

213
23:51.841 --> 23:53.034
Have you read the rules?

214
23:54.225 --> 23:56.061
Just follow them. That’s it.

215
23:57.232 --> 23:59.919
When I started, I learned everything on my own.

216
24:06.298 --> 24:07.540
How long have you been working here?

217
24:09.517 --> 24:10.748
Counting today,

218
24:11.947 --> 24:12.908
exactly seven days.

219
24:20.510 --> 24:21.909
This hasn’t expired yet, has it?

220
24:22.850 --> 24:24.178
Shouldn’t we separate it out first?

221
24:30.192 --> 24:31.122
You trying to teach me how to do my job?

222
24:34.483 --> 24:35.206
No.

223
24:36.124 --> 24:38.522
I just thought it’d be easier to check if we separated it.

224
24:49.365 --> 24:50.943
Don’t tell me how to do my job.

225
24:52.962 --> 24:54.438
Worry about surviving tonight yourself.

226
24:58.342 --> 24:59.678
If you’ve got so much free time,

227
25:00.303 --> 25:02.704
go restock the fridge.

228
25:05.920 --> 25:06.555
Go!

229
25:30.858 --> 25:32.218
Watermelon tea with dried fish.

230
25:32.934 --> 25:34.859
Mixed with sticky rice and boba.

231
25:38.264 --> 25:39.667
Does anyone actually drink this?

232
26:28.485 --> 26:31.432
(Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart. Please come again!)

233
26:38.505 --> 26:40.255
What on earth is this?

234
26:40.909 --> 26:43.810
You can’t even stack a few things without breaking them?

235
26:45.891 --> 26:47.656
Did a customer come into the store just now?

236
27:00.410 --> 27:01.354
What did you see?

237
27:05.679 --> 27:06.239
Nothing.

238
27:07.994 --> 27:08.900
Must have been my imagination.

239
27:12.463 --> 27:13.039
No.

240
27:14.479 --> 27:15.220
Here...

241
27:16.287 --> 27:17.568
There’s no such thing as “your imagination”

242
27:17.592 --> 27:18.618
or “seeing things.”

243
27:25.054 --> 27:25.619
Well...

244
27:27.041 --> 27:29.192
I think someone was standing in front of the drink fridge.

245
27:34.995 --> 27:35.661
That’s it?

246
27:40.528 --> 27:41.541
Rule number one.

247
27:43.402 --> 27:44.768
Rule number two.

248
27:46.853 --> 27:48.661
We didn't break any rules.

249
27:50.856 --> 27:51.768
Better safe than sorry.

250
27:54.984 --> 27:59.299
Protect me from evil, keep all harm away!

251
28:00.767 --> 28:01.716
What are you doing?

252
28:01.740 --> 28:02.580
Isn’t that a bit much?

253
28:04.368 --> 28:05.740
You think I’m joking?

254
28:06.454 --> 28:09.068
Believe it or not,

255
28:09.431 --> 28:10.734
that’s up to you.

256
28:12.485 --> 28:13.749
But don’t act like an idiot

257
28:13.774 --> 28:15.570
and get everyone else in trouble.

258
28:16.308 --> 28:17.443
You’ll bring us all down with you.

259
28:18.412 --> 28:20.197
Hey, enough!

260
28:20.927 --> 28:22.278
Are you going to fight in the store?

261
28:28.010 --> 28:29.260
Go take over the counter, too.

262
28:31.299 --> 28:32.680
He has no clue.

263
28:43.950 --> 28:44.846
I’ll do it myself.

264
29:28.274 --> 29:29.495
Hey, new guy!

265
29:30.434 --> 29:31.548
Take out the trash, too.

266
29:59.050 --> 29:59.883
Rule number nine.

267
30:00.707 --> 30:02.456
Employees must take the trash

268
30:02.480 --> 30:04.717
to the bins behind the store every day at 3 am.

269
31:09.388 --> 31:10.184
Oh, hey.

270
31:10.704 --> 31:11.900
You just started here?

271
31:12.436 --> 31:14.053
Yeah, it’s my first day.

272
31:15.362 --> 31:17.084
Hello, I’m Good.

273
31:18.009 --> 31:18.660
I’m Metha.

274
31:19.374 --> 31:20.244
Metha.

275
31:23.092 --> 31:24.190
Ready to unload the delivery?

276
31:24.590 --> 31:25.945
Sure. I’ll help.

277
31:35.947 --> 31:36.827
Here, take this.

278
31:41.553 --> 31:44.342
They didn’t order much today. Just this one box.

279
31:46.693 --> 31:49.199
Check the delivery and sign for it, too.

280
31:49.974 --> 31:50.997
Rule number 11.

281
31:51.679 --> 31:53.456
Employees must receive and inspect deliveries

282
31:53.481 --> 31:55.398
from the delivery truck at the designated time.

283
31:57.191 --> 31:58.037
It’s rough, bro.

284
31:58.751 --> 31:59.975
We’re short-staffed.

285
32:00.332 --> 32:02.054
People keep quitting after just a little while.

286
32:03.158 --> 32:03.756
Why’s that?

287
32:05.054 --> 32:06.494
Because they break the rules.

288
32:09.264 --> 32:09.787
Break the rules?

289
32:11.423 --> 32:12.742
Haven’t you heard the stories?

290
32:14.112 --> 32:15.120
I heard

291
32:17.069 --> 32:19.781
there was once a night-shift employee

292
32:20.476 --> 32:21.686
working here.

293
32:22.422 --> 32:24.257
Welcome to Sunny Mart.

294
32:25.558 --> 32:26.769
And that night...

295
32:27.848 --> 32:28.978
an old man came in.

296
32:33.682 --> 32:34.840
What can I get for you, sir?

297
32:43.576 --> 32:45.028
Could you please speak up?

298
32:48.078 --> 32:50.244
Speak louder, old man. I can't hear you.

299
32:51.508 --> 32:52.758
Kid...

300
32:53.502 --> 32:54.390
Yes?

301
33:03.812 --> 33:05.232
You tricked me!

302
33:09.904 --> 33:10.685
Open the door!

303
33:39.546 --> 33:40.340
You know

304
33:41.060 --> 33:43.183
why that employee died?

305
33:45.257 --> 33:46.580
His name was Noom.

306
33:47.513 --> 33:49.348
And he answered when the customer called him.

307
33:49.839 --> 33:52.713
Whoa! You’re good!

308
33:53.346 --> 33:54.590
You’re smart!

309
33:56.804 --> 33:58.217
How did you know that?

310
33:58.318 --> 34:00.431
Honestly, you’re the first person

311
34:00.455 --> 34:03.257
who’s gotten it right on the first try.

312
34:03.891 --> 34:04.942
You’re a genius!

313
34:06.414 --> 34:07.198
Wait a second.

314
34:07.891 --> 34:09.144
This story’s true, right?

315
34:09.283 --> 34:10.179
No, it’s not.

316
34:12.678 --> 34:13.393
I’m kidding.

317
34:13.670 --> 34:14.620
I don’t know.

318
34:14.967 --> 34:16.646
That’s just what people say, so I’m passing it on.

319
34:18.952 --> 34:20.268
Just something to keep us awake,

320
34:20.292 --> 34:21.480
relax, and relieve some stress.

321
34:24.405 --> 34:26.047
Aren’t you scared working here, though?

322
